  "title": "Tata Capital says revolving credit impact seen at 3-4% of AUM; alternate products being tested",
  "summary": "Tata Capital expects the impact of the Reserve Bank of India’s proposed curbs on revolving credit to be limited, with the NBFC estimating a 3-4% impact on its AUM, while it continues to engage with the regulator and evaluate alternate products. The non bank lender is looking at retail insurance products, higher NIM-plus-fee income and cost efficiencies to mitigate any potential hit to fee income from the proposed IRDAI distribution norms, MD & CEO Rajiv Sabharwal said.",
